\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x))\\left(-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}\\right)-\\int \\left(-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)}{2{x}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)}{2{x}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡(x)}{2{x}^{2}}+(-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)}{2{x}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}}+C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡(x)}{2{x}^{2}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)}{2{x}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}}(2{ln}^{2}⁡(x)+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+1)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539079 17592186576411 true] [17592186069262 1074 "We need to use integration by parts.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{2}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({ln}^{2}⁡(x))\\left(-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}\\right)-\\int \\left(-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}\\right)\\left(\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)}{x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡(x)}{2{x}^{2}}+\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)}{{x}^{3}}\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorna